# Update my skills

Resolve `scripts/update_skills.py` relative to this `SKILL.md`, then run it with Python 3. The request that triggered this skill authorizes the script's scoped Git fetch and local skill/instruction installation; request tool approval only when the environment requires it.

The script owns `~/.agents/repos/my-ai-skills` and symlinks every repository folder containing `SKILL.md` into `~/.agents/skills`. It validates and extracts the repository's `agents/Agent.md` instruction body before changing installed links, omitting its flat UAM frontmatter. It prepends that body to `${CODEX_HOME:-~/.codex}/AGENTS.md` inside a marked block while preserving machine-local instructions. It also refreshes a non-empty `AGENTS.override.md` so the override cannot suppress David's guidance. It backs up changed local entries, removes only stale symlinks into its managed checkout, and refuses to overwrite a dirty managed checkout.

Do not pull into the user's current project, edit skill contents, commit, push, delete unrelated local skills, or claim success after a partial run. Report the installed commit, skill count, backup path when present, removed stale links, and any blocker. Remind David to start a new Codex session so the refreshed `AGENTS.md` instruction chain is loaded.
